# The user's add-on disk: the images of the add-ons they installed (the Google apps, an ARM
# translation package, Widevine), which dsa-gapps.rc, dsa-arm-translation.rc and
# dsa-widevine-early.rc mount (Widevine's mounts the disk itself, earlier, at a point of its
# own, as apexd needs the module before post-fs). The host builds the disk, one per user, and attaches it to the VM read only; only the
# host changes it, when the user installs or removes an add-on, and the change takes effect at
# the next start. The host adds androidboot.dsa.addon_disk=on to the boot's bootconfig only
# while it attaches one.
#
# The disk holds one partition, dsa_addons, whose by-name link ueventd makes as it makes the
# links of every disk below the boot devices. The partition is an erofs file system that holds
# each add-on's erofs image as a plain, uncompressed file (gapps.img, arm-translation.img,
# widevine.img).
# Those images were kept on the user's disk, /data, until this disk: /data is encrypted, and
# ext4 gives no direct I/O to an encrypted file without inline encryption, so every page read
# from an image there was cached twice, once by the image file and once by erofs. The images
# are public packages with nothing to keep secret, and here erofs gives direct I/O to an
# uncompressed file, so the directio the scripts mount each image with takes effect.
#
# It is mounted before post-fs-data, where the scripts mount the images from it, and before
# /data, which it does not need. The files are labelled system files (context=), which init
# already reads, and the superblock gets a filesystem type of its own (fscontext=,
# sepolicy/addons.cil). Both go in one comma-separated argument: init passes only the last
# argument that is not a flag to the kernel, and context= alone relabels the superblock to a
# file type, which the kernel refuses. Nothing on the disk runs, so it is noexec too; the
# images mounted from it are mounts of their own and keep their own options.
on post-fs && property:ro.boot.dsa.addon_disk=on
    mkdir /mnt/dsa-addons 0755 root root
    mount erofs /dev/block/by-name/dsa_addons /mnt/dsa-addons ro nodev nosuid noexec fscontext=u:object_r:dsa_addons_fs:s0,context=u:object_r:system_file:s0
